      {
        "id": "p1-parser-1",
        "page": 1,
        "order": 1,
        "kind": "parser_text",
        "text": "Salt y. Tongues lightly with ordinary Salt, the next day with\nsource of salt peter, for 3 large tongues, or 4 small ones at the weeks\nend Salt them again with ordinary Salt, and let them lye a fortnight.\nThen Boils Boils them tender & peal them, take the root skins & the\nTelly part of the blade of the tongues. season them with Jamaica pepper\nbeaten, put them in a pot with 2 or 3 p. of Butter to Cor & Tongues so as\nto Cover them well, lay the roots at the top of the tongues to keep them\nmoist, covering them with double wet paper, tye them down, let them\nstand in the Oven about an hour & half, then take them out, swill\nthem in Butter to wash off the Spice & Settlement, put them in\nthe pot you intend to keep them in & after the Butter has stood to be\nClear from the Settlement, pour it upon them whilst it is hot & let\nthere be butter enough to Carry them of a Convenient Thickness.",
        "language": null,
        "writing": "unknown",
        "box": {
          "xyxy": [
            17.0,
            97.0,
            1500.0,
            1108.0
          ],
